   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T21:00:30Z",
   "body": "Fixed on [fix/5587-agent-test-running-isolation](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5587-agent-test-running-isolation), commit [81421adf](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/81421adfe5c003003a13ae6b4eb597d7b557f7d9), based on upstream `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe agent package's `TestMain` now holds the LiveAgent, OpenPencil and NewMax running guards false, alongside the existing OpenMausBot guard. Their own refusal tests still set the guards true; production process detection is unchanged.\n\nA controlled fake at the existing process-inspection seam makes each baseline guard see an app and fail the isolation check; all three pass after the change. The actual all-agent sync tests and four individual running-app refusal tests pass with `-race`; scoped vet and `go build -tags nogui ./...` pass. I independently reran the sync and refusal tests. The fake is not a live application, and no user process was started or stopped. Full-suite and cross-platform runtime checks were not run. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
